WEBVTT

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.000
<v Jordan>Have you guys seen this new podcast discovery app?

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.360
<v Jordan>It's called Dial Flipper and it's like an old time radio one.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.240
<v Jordan>I downloaded it.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.040
<v Jordan>It's really cool.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.679
<v Jordan>It's like a free app on an iOS.

00:00:09.679 --> 00:00:12.000
<v Jordan>I don't know if it's on Android too, probably.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Jordan>But what it is, is like you go in and you create an account and it asks you what your like favorite podcasts are and like what kind of topics you're into.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:32.240
<v Jordan>And then it does like an actual like dial where you hear the static of like the radio tuning and it'll take you to like different podcasts.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.200
<v Jordan>And so you can like them or flip them, and then you can like gather up different podcasts that you're interested in.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:43.679
<v Jordan>And it was actually really cool, but it was kind of weird because what it does is it drops you like right in the middle of the episode.

00:00:43.679 --> 00:00:49.439
<v Jordan>And so there were a few that dropped me like right in the middle of it, and it was like one of those like programmatic ads.

00:00:49.439 --> 00:00:51.439
<v Jordan>And so it felt a little, yeah.

00:00:51.439 --> 00:00:56.320
<v Jordan>And so it felt a little bit like when you're on the radio and you're like, oh, ad, and you're like skipping.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:56.960
<v Alban>Yeah.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.240
<v Alban>I like the concept.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.119
<v Alban>That's a good idea.

00:00:59.119 --> 00:01:05.599
<v Alban>That yeah, there have been times I've been driving and our local NPR affiliate is on.

00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:10.159
<v Alban>And I remember once listening to, I think it was Fresh Air with Terry Gross.

00:01:10.159 --> 00:01:15.840
<v Alban>I didn't know what it was, but it's a podcast episode and it's with somebody who sounds like a chef and it's really interesting.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.799
<v Alban>And he was traveling somewhere and he's telling this funny story, and then it turned out to be Anthony Bourdain.

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:25.680
<v Alban>And I think if you'd have told me it's Anthony Bourdain, I might have gone, this might be a good episode.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:33.680
<v Alban>But something about like being exposed to the whole story, it being interesting, and then finding out who the interviewer was, who the guest is.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:37.439
<v Alban>It's kind of nice to find to like discover podcasts that way.

00:01:37.599 --> 00:01:38.560
<v Kevin>It is a good idea.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:46.000
